{"title":"2003 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is isosceles, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3ac37c9fa391eebb9601bfaca8bfbfaabdf5ca1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/f/c9f1e7ea75793105974a6d9db5f4d88a7499f122.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC = 50^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/b/4cb9f317d225e8f825dde3b1102784c66bc43d74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAC = 60^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f336c86e6e7f7cf355f0363bd926e3e4f95675d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 70 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 50 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 80 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 60 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3ac37c9fa391eebb9601bfaca8bfbfaabdf5ca1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, we can see that angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/f/16f85b215ecbcc49698dd821f497369e79250cbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle ABC = m \\angle ACB = 50^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"219\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Next, the sum of the interior angles in a triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />. Applying this to triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840cb55c82434b9ae047760636a017e9441e6ca5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/e/fbee8319207c2b98f2f4c754e9d6dfe7c36da92a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 60^{\\circ} + 50^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"167\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/b/f5b8a337799665e71cb9353e0fc45bde2048ab50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 110^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"128\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/5/475d1bab13915eea11c3a57814a65a5ec9f1dbc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 180^{\\circ} - 110^{\\circ} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 70}^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"225\" height=\"31\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2003 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2003 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2003 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2003 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_